Deploy an ARM template to Azure
deploy in different ways 
  Deploy a local template
  Deploy a linked template
  Deploy in a continuous deployment pipeline

Resource group create commands (Azure CLI)
az group create --name {name of your resource group} --location "{location}"

Deployment group create (only works on latest version of CLI)-deploy resources under the resource group
templateFile="{provide-the-path-to-the-template-file}"
az deployment group create --name blanktemplate --resource-group myResourceGroup --template-file $templateFile

Deploy the ARM template with an output(Azure powershell)
$today=Get-Date -Format "MM-dd-yyyy"
$deploymentName="addOutputs-"+"$today"
New-AzResourceGroupDeployment -Name $deploymentName -TemplateFile $templateFile -storageName {your-unique-name} -storageSKU Standard_LRS


Microsoft Entra ID
-is part of the platform as a service (PaaS)
-is a comprehensive solution for managing identities, enforcing access policies, and securing your applications and data in the cloud and on-premises
-You can associate the same Microsoft Entra tenant with multiple Azure subscriptions. This allows you to use the same users, groups, and applications to manage resources across multiple Azure subscriptions.
-A single Microsoft Entra tenant can support multiple Azure subscriptions.
